Z||000007||LAMBO||09-07-2000||09:24 AM||||It came from Fort Macalevy(sp?) just south of State College. Absolutely beautiful country down there. A driving paradise for someone with a properly set up Fiero, winding roads, mountains, ahhhhh. The car is almost perfect. Only major flaws are one cracked rocker fx, broken timing gear and chain(fixing this weekend) and a little paint fading on top hood only, Everything else is shiney black. Tires only had 3k miles on them. Everything works (that I could tell without motor running). Needless to say, I can't wait to get her on the road. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Once shes running, I will probably be selling my 86 GT 4sp for what I have in it (under $2k). Let me know if anyones interested.<BR>Lambo||||reg||1
Z||000008||fiero56||09-07-2000||02:44 PM||||You just have to rub it in, don't you LAMBO. That was going to be MY Fiero, but I was a little too late. I was #4 in the waiting list <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> If you took I-70 through Ohio, you drive within about 30 miles of me. If you ever want to sell it for what you paid for it, I'll buy it.<P>Good job on the deal. The owner told me he had a lot of people(45) inquire about it in 2 days. Congrats.||||reg||1
